<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gaius Suetonius Paulinus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st century</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a> · Also known as Suetonius Paulinus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gaius <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suetonius">Suetonius</a> Paulinus was a Roman general and governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> from about 58 to 61 CE. He campaigned in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a> against tribes such as the Ordovices and attacked the druid centre on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglesey">Anglesey</a> in 60 CE. He then returned to defeat the revolt of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boudica">Boudica</a> and the Iceni, after which he was recalled.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gaius-suetonius-paulinus.jpg" alt="Gaius Suetonius Paulinus" width="320" height="421" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ad Meskens · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Roman_baths_suetonius_paulinus_02.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
